WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.730
Eleven o'clock, Monday morning.

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.240
A hall in New Delhi.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.400
A country was about to start

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.050
writing itself down.

5
00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.967
The Constituent Assembly

6
00:00:10.967 --> 00:00:14.187
Debates, volume one, record it.

7
00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:16.354
The ninth of December, nineteen

8
00:00:16.354 --> 00:00:19.457
forty six, in Constitution Hall.

9
00:00:19.907 --> 00:00:21.407
Two hundred and seven members

10
00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:24.207
came. The Muslim League, which

11
00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:26.267
had won seventy three seats,

12
00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.367
stayed away.

13
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.797
Those seats stayed empty.

14
00:00:30.345 --> 00:00:33.176
Someone had to open the sitting.

15
00:00:33.176 --> 00:00:35.425
Acharya Kripalani asked the

16
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:37.140
oldest member, Doctor

17
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.405
Sachchidananda Sinha, to take

18
00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:40.315
the chair.

19
00:00:41.076 --> 00:00:42.516
He thanked them.

20
00:00:42.516 --> 00:00:44.616
Then he said they had chosen

21
00:00:44.616 --> 00:00:47.196
him, in his words, "on the sole

22
00:00:47.196 --> 00:00:49.556
ground that I am in age, the

23
00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:51.136
senior most member of this

24
00:00:51.136 --> 00:00:54.376
Assembly." A modest start.

25
00:00:54.376 --> 00:00:56.916
Few leaders open by naming their

26
00:00:56.916 --> 00:00:58.386
only qualification.

27
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:00.790
He listed the work ahead:

28
00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.220
a permanent president, rules,

29
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.820
committees. And he wished the

30
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.300
Assembly wisdom, toleration,

31
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.750
justice, and fairness to all.

32
00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:13.251
Then came the register.

33
00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:14.911
Members presented their

34
00:01:14.911 --> 00:01:16.811
credentials, and signed their

35
00:01:16.811 --> 00:01:18.861
names, one by one.

36
00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.174
The Assembly adjourned until

37
00:01:21.174 --> 00:01:23.704
Tuesday, eleven o'clock.

38
00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:25.454
For GS2:

39
00:01:25.454 --> 00:01:27.254
the Constituent Assembly first

40
00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:28.954
met on nine December nineteen

41
00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:30.434
forty six, with Dr.

42
00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:34.314
Sinha, the oldest member, as

43
00:01:34.314 --> 00:01:34.974
temporary chairman.

44
00:01:34.974 --> 00:01:37.474
The Muslim League stayed away.

45
00:01:37.474 --> 00:01:39.874
Rajendra Prasad was elected

46
00:01:39.874 --> 00:01:41.304
president later.

47
00:01:42.337 --> 00:01:44.337
The hall was not full.

48
00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.647
The work began anyway.
